From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Tiziano=20M=C3=BCller?= <tiziano.mueller@hpe.com>
Date: Tue, 25 Mar 2026 10:00:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] kmp_files: use /usr/lib/modules for usr-merged distros
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

On distributions with usr-merge (e.g. openSUSE Leap 16.0), the kernel
installs modules under /usr/lib/modules/ rather than /lib/modules/.
The modules_install make target writes to the correct usr-merged path,
but the kmp_files template still references /lib/modules/%2-%1, causing
rpmbuild to fail with "File not found" when packaging KMP subpackages:

  error: File not found: .../BUILDROOT/.../lib/modules/6.12.0-...-default/...
  error: File not found: .../BUILDROOT/.../lib/modules/6.12.0-...-64kb/...

Use the %{kernel_module_directory} RPM macro -- the same macro the
default %kernel_module_package file list uses -- so the path resolves
to /usr/lib/modules on usr-merged systems and /lib/modules on
traditional layouts.

Signed-off-by: Tiziano Mueller <tiziano.mueller@hpe.com>
---
 kmp_files | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/kmp_files b/kmp_files
index 1234567..abcdefg 100644
--- a/kmp_files
+++ b/kmp_files
@@ -1,3 +1,3 @@
 %defattr (-,root,root)
-/lib/modules/%2-%1
+%{kernel_module_directory}/%2-%1
 /usr/bin/rxe_init.sh
